<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Redbad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 719</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Radbod, King of the Frisians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Redbad, also Radbod, was king of the Frisians from about 680 until his death in 719. He fought the Frankish mayors of the palace, losing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorestad">Dorestad</a> and Utrecht to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pippin-of-herstal">Pippin of Herstal</a> around 690, but after Pippin's death in 714 he recovered them and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> in 716. He opposed the Christian missions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willibrord">Willibrord</a> and Boniface, and later legend made him a symbol of Frisian independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/redbad.jpg" alt="Redbad" width="320" height="586" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sonty567 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Radboud_doopvont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
